'''''Pachystachys lutea''''', known as the '''golden shrimp plant''' or '''lollipop plant''',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sahani |first=Rani |title=Lollipop plant – Care, Uses, Propagation (Best info IN 2024) |url=https://lollipopplant.com/lollipop-plant-lollipop-tree |website=Lollipop plant|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240507200811/https://lollipopplant.com/lollipop-plant-lollipop-tree/|archive-date=May 7, 2024}}</ref> is a tropical, soft-stemmed evergreen shrub between 0.5 and 2.5 meters tall, native to [[Peru]].<ref name=":0">{{cite web|url=http://hort.ifas.ufl.edu/shrubs/PACLUTA.PDF|title=Pachystachys lutea|author1=Edward F. Gilman|author2=Alan Meerow|date=October 1999|website=Hort.ifas.ufl.edu|access-date=24 March 2022}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal|last=Wasshausen|first=D. C.|date=1986|title=The systematics of the genus Pachystachys (Acanthaceae)|journal=Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington|volume=99|issue=1|pages=160–185}}</ref> The [[zygomorphic]], long-throated, short-lived white flowers emerge sequentially from overlapping bright yellow [[bract]]s on [[raceme]]s that are produced throughout the warm months.<ref name=":0" />

The Latin [[binomial nomenclature|specific epithet]] ''lutea'' means "yellow".<ref name=RHSLG>{{cite book |last=Harrison |first=Lorraine |title=RHS Latin for Gardeners |year=2012 |publisher=Mitchell Beazley |location=United Kingdom |isbn=978-1845337315 }}</ref>

It is cultivated as an ornamental, but in cold temperate regions it requires protection from temperatures below {{convert|10|C|F|abbr=on}}.<ref name="RHSPF" /> It has won the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref name="RHSPF">{{cite web|title=RHS Plantfinder - Pachystachys lutea|url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/74937/i-Pachystachys-lutea-i/Details|website=Rhs.org.uk|access-date=14 April 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url= https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/agm-lists/agm-ornamentals.pdf | title = AGM Plants - Ornamental | date = July 2017 | page = 71 | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | access-date = 14 April 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Jhon |first1=Dolphy |title=Free plant identification app |url=https://letplant.com/insights/free-plant-identification-apps/ |access-date=17 August 2024}}</ref>

